{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "\"the social network\" is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the consequences that followed. directed by david fincher, the movie is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich. the screenplay was written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his witty and engaging dialogue.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard, being dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright (played by rooney mara). in an attempt to cope with his emotions, mark creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes an instant hit, but also gets mark into trouble with the university.\n\nlater, mark is approached by twin brothers, cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are looking to create a social networking site for harvard students. mark agrees to help them, but eventually decides to create his own site, which he calls \"thefacebook\". with the help of his friend eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield), mark is able to get the site off the ground and it quickly becomes a huge success.\n\nas the site grows in popularity, mark and eduardo's friendship begins to fray. eduardo, who is the chief financial officer of the company, becomes increasingly frustrated with mark's lack of business acumen and his tendency to make decisions without consulting him. meanwhile, mark becomes more and more focused on expanding the site and making it a success, even if it means sacrificing his relationships with his friends.\n\nthe film also explores the lawsuit filed by the winklevoss twins, who claim that mark stole their idea. the twins are portrayed as entitled and arrogant, and their lawsuit is seen as a attempt to get a piece of the action.\n\nthe cast of \"the social network\" is excellent. jesse eisenberg gives a nuanced performance as mark zuckerberg, capturing his awkwardness and intensity. andrew garfield is also good as eduardo saverin, bringing a sense of vulnerability and naivety to the role. justin timberlake, who plays sean parker, the co-founder of napster, is also memorable, bringing a sense of charisma and confidence to the role.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy. it's a haunting and atmospheric soundtrack that perfectly captures the mood of the film.\n\none of the strengths of \"the social network\" is its writing. aaron sorkin's dialogue is witty and engaging, and the film's script is full of clever observations about the characters and their motivations. the film also raises interesting questions about the nature of success and the costs of ambition.\n\noverall, \"the social network\" is a compelling and thought-provoking film that is well worth watching. it's a film that is both entertaining and insightful, and it's a great example of how a well-made film can be both a commercial success and a critical darling.", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.7056629657745361}, {"token": "the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " social", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -6.556489552167477e-06}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -1.8067126274108887}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.03177696093916893}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -1.9763846397399902}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -3.6954811548639555e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -7.867782187531702e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0067178355529904366}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.001106127048842609}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0015023384476080537}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0